; Procedural typed constants and initialized variables: nil, @F of a
; routine at program or unit level (or a static method), or a lambda that
; uses nothing of the routines around it and has no object.
; RUN: not %p3 --mode=objfpc -ferror-limit=0 -c %S/Inputs/constlambdas/errors.pas -o %t.o 2>&1 | FileCheck %s
; CHECK: errors.pas:12:14: error: typed constant value must be a constant: this lambda's object is Self
; CHECK: errors.pas:18:12: error: typed constant value must be a constant: this lambda uses 'k' of the routine around it
; CHECK: errors.pas:20:12: error: initial value must be a constant: this lambda uses 'k' of the routine around it
; CHECK: errors.pas:26:13: error: '@Inner': only routines declared at program or unit level can be procedural values
; CHECK: errors.pas:31:12: error: typed constants of type 'TFn' can only be initialized with nil, a routine or a lambda
; CHECK: errors.pas:32:28: error: typed constants of type 'TFn' can only be initialized with nil, a routine or a lambda
; CHECK: errors.pas:33:12: error: this lambda has 2 parameters, but 'TFn' is wanted here
; CHECK: errors.pas:34:14: error: cannot initialize 'TCalc' with a value of type 'function(string): integer of object'
; CHECK-NOT: error:
;
; The code: {function, nil}, set once the routines are declared.
; RUN: %p3 --mode=objfpc --emit-llvm %S/../run/constlambdas.pas -o %t.ll
; RUN: FileCheck --check-prefix=IR %s < %t.ll
; RUN: opt -passes=verify -disable-output %t.ll
; IR: @pas.ident = internal global { ptr, ptr } { ptr @pas.id, ptr null }
; IR: @pas.twice = internal global { ptr, ptr } { ptr @"pas.$lambda1", ptr null }
